{"id": "015_loop", "time": "2026-11-25T06:42:38", "status": "accepted", "hypothesis": "Halving the base learning rate from 0.4 to 0.2 should give better-conditioned features on every seed, because doubling it in 014_loop clearly hurt, and lowering it continues that trend in the helpful direction. In 014_loop, going 0.4→0.8 cost 3.7 points on seed 42, and effective rank fell from 182.7 to 147.9. With the 200-step warmup in place, the optimum for this 20-epoch run looks to sit at or below 0.4, and a smaller step should keep more feature dimensions in use.", "parent": "013_loop", "category": "optimisation", "basis": "both - known (solo-learn's CIFAR Barlow Twins recipe uses a base LR of about 0.3 with scale_loss 0.1) plus results from 013_loop and 014_loop (the LR trend, and effective rank dropping as LR rose).", "scores": {"42": 0.39159220457077026, "43": 0.41906654834747314, "44": 0.37106919288635254}, "val_acc": 0.39390931526819867, "best_before": 0.3441465397675832, "seconds": 4629.5, "error": null, "changes": [["-", "'lr': 0.4,"], ["+", "'lr': 0.2,"]], "loss_curve": [30.4375, 77.5682, 97.8352, 86.3972, 79.6664, 72.0659, 67.2728, 62.2508, 58.1219, 55.149, 52.007, 49.7078, 47.6181, 45.8967, 44.2513, 42.8682, 41.7188, 40.8615, 40.6146, 40.2871], "features": {"finite": true, "dim": 512, "effective_rank": 189.0, "mean_std": 0.4918}, "pretrain_loss": "30.4375 -> 40.2871", "explore": false, "llm": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "system_prompt": "You are a machine learning researcher. Answer with text only, exactly in the reply format the user asks for.", "seconds": 28.6, "model_usage": {"claude-haiku-5-5": {"inputTokens": 6465, "outputTokens": 34, "cacheReadInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 0, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.0006635, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 0, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-5-5", "provider":